
# Student Management System

A simple CRUD web application built with Go, HTML, CSS, MySQL,
Docker, Docker Compose, Jenkins and AWS EC2.

## Architecture

- Frontend: HTML, CSS and Nginx
- Backend: Go REST API
- Database: MySQL 8.4
- Containerization: Docker
- Local orchestration: Docker Compose
- CI/CD: Jenkins
- Deployment: AWS EC2

## Features

- Add a student
- View all students
- Update student details
- Delete a student
- Persist records in MySQL

## Run locally

1. Install Docker Desktop.
2. Open a terminal in the project root.
3. Start the application:

   docker compose up -d --build

4. Open http://localhost:8080

## Useful commands

Check services:

    docker compose ps

View logs:

    docker compose logs -f

Stop services:

    docker compose down

Rebuild after code changes:

    docker compose up -d --build

## API endpoints

| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|--------|----------|-------------|
| GET | /api/students | List students |
| POST | /api/students | Create student |
| PUT | /api/students/{id} | Update student |
| DELETE | /api/students/{id} | Delete student |
| GET | /health | Backend health check |

## Database

Database: student_db
Table: students

Example query:

    SELECT * FROM students;

## CI/CD plan

GitHub -> Jenkins CI -> Docker Hub -> Jenkins CD -> AWS EC2

The CI pipeline tests the Go application and builds and pushes
the frontend and backend images.

The CD pipeline pulls the images and deploys them using
the production Docker Compose configuration.
